  "description": "What sauerkraut is to a dog and kimchi is to a Korean pancake, curtido is to a variety of Latin American dishes. Traditional curtido is prepared days in advance of when it'll be eaten, enabling it to develop a fermented tang. This shortcut version is a nice fallback when you don't have time to think ahead.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 1 hr 10 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: 1 small jalapeño, ribs and seeds removed, minced (optional)\n\nNotes: Curtido is ready within 1 hour, but improves with time. It can be stored in airtight containers in the refrigerator for up to one month.",
